  <issue>
  Fix duplicated metric data on query_hash collision
Sentry should not send more than one query spec per project using the same `query_hash` tag value.

## Details

To collect unique metrics for every alert or dashboard widget, Sentry computes a query hash from the selected field and filters. This hash is supposed to be unique to the query. It is meant to be reused, so that if two alerts or widgets require the same metric, it can be extracted exactly once.

The query hash is used as a tag in a metric with fixed MRI. Through that, Sentry queries the metric filtered by the tag value, to get the unique time series of the alert or widget.

However, Sentry potentially sends the same query hash multiple times to Relay, which then extracts values for that metric multiple times. Particularly in counters, this leads to wrong values, as a single event is counted multiple times.

## Potential Fix

While Relay could de-duplicate these metrics, it does not have any semantic understanding of the `query_hash` tag. Therefore, the Sentry project config module should de-duplicate on-demand metrics based on their query_hash. 

This de-duplication should occur at project boundary. If two project-specific metrics in an organization share the same `query_hash`, they are still sent to different projects, and the product can query them appropriately. If there is an organization-level metric (such as a dashboard widget), the deduplication can occur individually for every project.
  </issue>
  
